  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The given pair makes the ratio \\(\\frac{3\\cdot2-4}{3+15}=\\frac{1}{9}.\\) Therefore, when \\(y=12,\\) \\[ \\frac{3x-4}{27}=\\frac19, \\] so \\(3x-4=3\\) and \\(x=\\frac{7}{3}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(x=2\\) and \\(y=3\\) to find the constant ratio",
        "Keep \\(\\frac{3x-4}{y+15}\\) equal to that ratio when \\(y=12\\)"
      ],
